As a developer, I want make to issue nice concise output for each target, instead of dumping unwieldly commands.

eg. Instead of dumping:

emacs --batch \
	    --eval "(setq org-confirm-babel-evaluate nil)" \
	    --eval "(setq org-export-with-broken-links t)" \
	    --eval "(setq org-latex-pdf-process '(\"xelatex -interaction=nonstopmode -output-directory=%o %f\" \"xelatex -interaction=nonstopmode -output-directory=%o %f\"))" \
	    "documentation/alfe--specifications.org" \
	    --funcall org-latex-export-to-pdf

it could display:

[emacs producing pdf from documentation/alfe--specifications.org]


A DEBUG flag would make make display the whole commands again.

Low priority, we'll do that at the end, when everything is mostly debugged and we don't need the whole commands.

* DEFERRED 2026-08-11 — on the ticket's own condition

Reached in the P3 pass and deliberately left. "At the end, when
everything is mostly debugged" is not yet true (the =compiler= and
=drawing-database-api= epics are open, and the native macOS/Windows CI
lanes are still being brought up), and this session gave two concrete
counter-examples where the raw command dump was exactly what made a
failure diagnosable: the ASDF =MISSING-DEPENDENCY= for babel in
=run-file-compat/launch.lisp=, and the interactor framework's
command-key rejection during the =lisp-configuration= work. CI logs are
also the main debugging surface for the runners pjb cannot easily reach.

* Sizing, for when it is picked up

~1040 recipe lines across 7 Makefiles (clautolisp 290,
autolisp-front-end 180, root 211, autolisp-test 111, autolisp-spec 78,
autolisp-benchmark 65, documentation 5), with no shared include and no
existing quiet infrastructure.

Cheapest correct shape:

- a =make/quiet.mk= included by all seven (single source of truth),
  holding =.SILENT:= under =ifeq ($(DEBUG),)= — one line silences the
  echoing of every recipe in a Makefile without touching the 1040 lines,
  and it suppresses only the *echo*, not the commands' own output;
- per-target =@echo '[…]'= messages on the targets worth announcing,
  added where they earn their place rather than everywhere — a silent
  long build otherwise looks hung;
- =DEBUG=1= set globally in =.gitlab-ci.yml= =variables:= and the GitHub
  workflow =env:= (one line each), so CI logs keep the full commands
  while interactive use gets the concise output. That is what makes the
  deferral rationale above moot when the time comes.
